      "type": "give_medication",
      "args": {
        "medication_code": "unknown",
        "dose": "standard"
      },
      "justification": "DKA patients are typically total body potassium-depleted. Per ADA guidelines, potassium replacement is required if K+ < 5.3 mEq/L before starting insulin. Insulin will drive potassium intracellularly, risking life-threatening hypokalemia. Must replace before initiating insulin infusion."
    },
    {
